Another thing, looking at the code
https://github.com/ibm-bioinformatics/BlueSNP/blob/master/src/R/MapReduce/read_plink_tped.R

If reduce is not specified or is just a number >0 e.g.
rhwatch(map, reduce=10)

then an identity reduce is used and there will be 10 reduce tasks.
reduce = 10 is identical to mapred.reduce.tasks=10

if reduce=0,e.g. rhwatch(map, reduce=0) then it will be a map only job.
If you have a custom reducer, only then should you write reduce=reduce (and specify mapred.reduce.tasks in the mapred argument if you want to control it)

