Lets go simpler,

0. Create a tmp directory (on the HDFS) readable by the user (under which the hadoop job will run)
e.g. /user/sguha/tmp
1. rhoptions(HADOOP.TMP.FOLDER=path-to-temp-folder)
(RHIPE creates a lot of rhipe-temp* files in this folder, clean the files using rhclean)

2.Set a working directory and copy a small text file to the HDFS

hdfs.setwd("/user/sguha/")

rhput("~/in2.r","my.text.file")

rhread("my.text.file",type='text')

3. Try this
z <- rhwatch(map=rhmap( rhcollect(k,r) ), reduce=0, input=rhfmt("my.text.file",type='text'),read=FALSE)
rhread(z)

